Adds up a list of integers, with a recursive function defined by letrec.
The input is a list, and a number is not a list, so an integer input is an error.
---
(lam xs (letrec sum (lam l (if (? l) 0 (+ (head l) (sum (tail l))))) (sum xs)))
---
~ => 0 fuel 1000
[5 ~] => 5 fuel 1000
[1 [2 [3 ~]]] => 6 fuel 10000
0 => error fuel 1000
